Among the following judgments:  
(1) The proposition "If q then p" and "If not p then not q" are contrapositives of each other;  
(2) "am<sup>2</sup> < bm<sup>2</sup>" is a necessary and sufficient condition for "a < b";  
(3) The negation of the proposition "The diagonals of a rectangle are equal" is a false proposition;  
(4) The proposition "∅⊆{1,2}" is true, the correct sequence numbers are.

s:
Based on the definition of contrapositive, (1) is correct;  
Since when m=0, m<sup>2</sup>=0, if a<b then am<sup>2</sup><bm<sup>2</sup> is a false proposition, hence (2) is incorrect;  
Since the negation is: The diagonals of a quadrilateral that is not a rectangle are not equal, and the diagonals of an isosceles trapezoid are equal, which is not a rectangle, hence (3) is incorrect;  
Since ∅ is a subset of any set, therefore (4) is correct;  
Thus, the answer is $\boxed{(1)(4)}$.

